# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Obsolete Vite-era files — excluded from the Vercel build.
#
# These files remain on disk but are NOT imported anywhere in the live Next.js
# app. They are leftovers from the Vite → Next.js migration and BREAK `next build`
# if included in the deployment:
#
#   • src/pages/**  — Next.js treats a `src/pages` directory as the Pages Router
#     and compiles every file into a route. These files still import the removed
#     `react-router-dom` and use `import.meta.env`, so the build fails.
#   • src/routes/{AppRoutes,publicRoutes,adminRoutes}.tsx — old react-router route
#     tables that also import `react-router-dom`.
#   • src/routes/types.ts — types used only by those dead route tables.
#
# RECOMMENDED: delete these from the repository (see the migration report). Once
# deleted, every line below becomes a harmless no-op and this file can be removed.
# The live App Router lives entirely under src/app/**, which is NOT ignored.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
src/pages
src/routes/AppRoutes.tsx
src/routes/publicRoutes.tsx
src/routes/adminRoutes.tsx
src/routes/types.ts
